## Attribution that travels with the crate

The crate as a whole is original to this project, written from published specifications and from
black-box measurement of sacreBLEU's observable output (`docs/spec/` in the repository records each
one). One file is the disclosed exception:

* `src/ter_clean.rs`, the candidate-budget and shift-selection semantics of the TER shift search, is
  derived from sacreBLEU's `sacrebleu/metrics/lib_ter.py`, Copyright 2020 Memsource, licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0. That derivation was made on the copyright holder's instruction
  after black-box probing showed the published algorithm did not reproduce the oracle.

If you take this crate under the MIT option, that file's Apache-2.0 attribution obligations still
travel with it: keep this notice and `LICENSE-APACHE` alongside any redistribution. Taking the crate
under Apache-2.0 satisfies them by construction, which is why the dual grant is offered.

The generated tables in `src/tables.rs` are built by `tools/gen_tables.py` from the running CPython's
Unicode database and the `regex` module's property data. Python's Unicode data is distributed under
the Unicode License Agreement; the `regex` crate is MIT/Apache-2.0.